IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rtad-drivers`
IMPORT `rtad-qa`

-- Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (rtad-qa.l4): every exported question,
-- for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it
-- is an assumed term"). Each question with a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the situation's one value
-- that does not hold (FALSE), every later input ASSUMEd, and must answer `does not arise for you`. For the learner and
-- driver, where the situation holds, each question is asked on facts worked by hand from the deposited text, and once
-- more against the baseline export's own answer on the same facts.
--
-- One limit (graffiti finding 31): the baseline reads `Supervisor`, `Night purpose`, `How I am disqualified`, `What I
-- was convicted of` and `How my offence ended` through OTHERWISE, so for those enumerations an ASSUMEd value read is not
-- caught. Every situation input is a BOOLEAN, read before anything else, and the role is read first; the parameter
-- script checks the order (NOTES.md).
--
-- Facts are the baseline's (rtad-cases-drivers.l4): Chloe born 14 March 2003, permit 14 March 2019, licence 14 March
-- 2020; Jake born 30 August 2006, licence 30 August 2023, 25 km/h over on 19 July 2049. HYPOTHETICAL: the supervisors,
-- logbooks, passengers and notices.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked supervisor` IS A Supervisor
ASSUME `an unasked standing` IS A `My standing to supervise`
ASSUME `an unasked purpose` IS A `Night purpose`
ASSUME `an unasked way of being disqualified` IS A `How I am disqualified`
ASSUME `an unasked conviction` IS A `What I was convicted of`
ASSUME `an unasked offence` IS A `Road Traffic Act offence`
ASSUME `an unasked outcome` IS A `How my offence ended`
ASSUME `an unasked learning drive` IS A `My learning drive`
ASSUME `an unasked experience` IS A `My driving experience`
ASSUME `an unasked set of passengers` IS A `My passengers`
ASSUME `an unasked drive` IS A `My drive`

`as the driver` MEANS `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence`
`as the supervisor` MEANS `I supervise a learner driver, or ride with a new driver`

`a licensed driver` MEANS `I hold an Australian driver licence or a foreign driving authorisation for this kind of driving`
`an instructor` MEANS `I hold a driving instructor's licence (Motor Vehicle Drivers Instructors Act 1963)`
`a course instructor` MEANS `I am an instructor in a youth driver education course run or supervised by a body the CEO authorised`
`not licensed for it` MEANS `I hold only a learner's permit for it, or no licence for it`

`Chloe driving with her father beside her` MEANS `My learning drive` WITH
    `my permit is in force` IS TRUE
    `I am driving solely to learn` IS TRUE
    `my supervisor` IS `another licensed driver`
    `years my supervisor has held a licence for this kind of driving` IS 30
    `I am learning to ride a moped` IS FALSE
    `my supervisor accompanies me` IS TRUE

`Chloe driving alone on her permit` MEANS `My learning drive` WITH
    `my permit is in force` IS TRUE
    `I am driving solely to learn` IS TRUE
    `my supervisor` IS `another licensed driver`
    `years my supervisor has held a licence for this kind of driving` IS 30
    `I am learning to ride a moped` IS FALSE
    `my supervisor accompanies me` IS FALSE

`Chloe's logbook and tests` MEANS `My driving experience` WITH
    `my date of birth` IS (Date 14 3 2003)
    `the day my learner's permit was granted` IS (Date 14 3 2019)
    `supervised hours logged` IS 52
    `of them, night hours` IS 6
    `logged in an approved logbook, signed by my supervisors` IS TRUE
    `I passed the hazard perception test` IS TRUE
    `the day of the hazard perception test` IS (Date 16 9 2019)
    `I passed the practical driving assessment` IS TRUE
    `the day of the practical driving assessment` IS (Date 14 3 2020)

`three school friends` MEANS `My passengers` WITH
    `number of passengers, counting any co-driver` IS 3
    `years the most experienced passenger has held a non-provisional licence for my class` IS 0
    `every passenger after the first is immediate family` IS FALSE
    `my employer requires me to carry them, and I carry the employer's signed document` IS FALSE

`Jake riding his motorcycle on his licence` MEANS `My drive` WITH
    `my licence or permit covers this class of vehicle` IS TRUE
    `it is current, not suspended or cancelled, and not obtained while disqualified` IS TRUE
    `I am disqualified from holding or obtaining a licence` IS FALSE
    `I am breaking a Schedule 7 condition (A, B, E, I, N, S or Z)` IS FALSE
    `I am breaking a novice night-time or passenger restriction` IS FALSE
    `on a learner's permit, my supervisor is with me or I hold no permit` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle needs no licence under r 55` IS FALSE
    `the CEO gave me a written permit for this driving` IS FALSE

`Jake riding while disqualified` MEANS `My drive` WITH
    `my licence or permit covers this class of vehicle` IS TRUE
    `it is current, not suspended or cancelled, and not obtained while disqualified` IS TRUE
    `I am disqualified from holding or obtaining a licence` IS TRUE
    `I am breaking a Schedule 7 condition (A, B, E, I, N, S or Z)` IS FALSE
    `I am breaking a novice night-time or passenger restriction` IS FALSE
    `on a learner's permit, my supervisor is with me or I hold no permit` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle needs no licence under r 55` IS FALSE
    `the CEO gave me a written permit for this driving` IS FALSE

